+++ b/docs/ui-main-material-20261027.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Shared main-area material continuation
+
+After the ordinary parameter cards were unified, sequence marks, arrangement/settings rows and remaining MIX wells still used the earlier flat surfaces. This applies the same shallow material vocabulary inside their existing geometry.
+
+Drum hits, captured synth note lengths, and the selected voice keep their existing colours and data positions. Compact marks retain their centre ink; p-lock notches, play indication, ties and slides are overlaid on the original paths. SONG keeps its dense row count and scrolling. GLOBAL/list rows keep their fonts, values, arrows and confirmations. MIX PARTS/MASTER keep exact meters, level positions, names, gain-reduction and load values. No control remapping, new feature, optional SONG density change, audio/storage work or boot geometry change.
+
+The affected host fixture renders populated drum/synth/song, a tie across the 16/17 page boundary, muted active MIX, MASTER and selected/scrolled settings rows. Reset confirmation is opened for rendering only; reset is not executed. Project bytes are asserted unchanged. Compact marks are checked across widths1..14 and heights4..10 for clipping and retained centre ink. Existing SMC UI and stable part-order suites cover original interaction mappings.
+
+Actual candidate previews, commands and receipts are in sibling `ui-main-material-evidence-20261027`. Independent review and owner preview remain separate pending stages; no native build, hardware, rollout or final boot render is claimed here.
diff --git a/docs/ui-shared-glyph-20261027.md b/docs/ui-shared-glyph-20261027.md
